{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"114075","commit":"d7747da0fe34fe856504fac85091a1fb1025e82e","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for updating the `took` time and status for remote clusters is duplicated across multiple methods (`updateExecutionInfoAfterCoordinatorOnlyQuery`, `acquireCompute`, and `updateTookTimeForRemoteClusters`). This duplication can lead to inconsistencies and maintenance challenges. Consider refactoring this common logic into a single method that can be reused by these functions.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java--14978:16221","promptId":"#4CX2R","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":14978,"endPos":16221,"startLine":310,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":330,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1244}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java--12365:13563","promptId":"#VKNJD","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":12365,"endPos":13563,"startLine":254,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":272,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1199}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java-8358:8400,8598:8674-8270:8328,8429:8434,8632:8884,9021:9026","promptId":"#1GW2J","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeService.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":8358,"endPos":8400,"startLine":176,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":176,"endLineOffset":62,"length":43},{"pos":8598,"endPos":8674,"startLine":181,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":181,"endLineOffset":114,"length":77}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":8270,"endPos":8328,"startLine":174,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":174,"endLineOffset":70,"length":59},{"pos":8429,"endPos":8434,"startLine":177,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":177,"endLineOffset":25,"length":6},{"pos":8632,"endPos":8884,"startLine":182,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":185,"endLineOffset":21,"length":253},{"pos":9021,"endPos":9026,"startLine":188,"startLineOffset":101,"endLine":188,"endLineOffset":106,"length":6}]}]},{"comment":"The use of `System.nanoTime()` to calculate the duration in both methods (`updateExecutionInfoAfterCoordinatorOnlyQuery` and `updateTookTimeForRemoteClusters`) assumes that the system clock does not change during the query execution. While this is generally true, it\u0027s worth noting that `System.nanoTime()` is more suitable for measuring elapsed time than `System.currentTimeMillis()`. However, ensure that the start time (`queryStartNanos`) is consistently captured and used across all relevant methods.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java--14978:16221","promptId":"#4CX2R","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":14978,"endPos":16221,"startLine":310,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":330,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1244}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/ComputeServi