difies `clustersWithNoMatchingIndices` by removing elements from `indexResolution.getUnavailableClusters()`. This operation is correct but could be optimized for performance. Using `removeAll` on a set can be inefficient if the set being removed from (`clustersWithNoMatchingIndices`) is large and the set being used to remove (`indexResolution.getUnavailableClusters()`) is also large, as it involves checking each element in `clustersWithNoMatchingIndices` against all elements in `indexResolution.getUnavailableClusters()`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java--14080:14162","promptId":"#47TC7","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/session/EsqlSession.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":14080,"endPos":14162,"startLine":290,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":290,"endLineOffset":90,"length":83}]}]},{"comment":"The changes to the test cases update the expected size of the result map from 2 to 3, which suggests that the `runEsql` method now returns an additional key-value pair in the result map. The new assertion checks that the value associated with the \"took\" key is a non-negative integer. This change implies that the `runEsql` method has been modified to include execution time information in its response.\nHowever, the changes do not provide any context or documentation about why this additional key (\"took\") was added and what it represents. It would be beneficial to add comments or update the method\u0027s documentation to clarify this change and ensure that other developers understand the new behavior of `runEsql`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/qa/rest/RestEsqlTestCase.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/server/src/main/java/org/el